  "id": "Compound::DB01241 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "Gemfibrozil is known to bind to Cyp2c9, which is involved in the oxidation of various substrates, including quinones and aromatic compounds. This binding leads to Cyp2c9 participating in the oxidoreductase activity, which is subsequently participated by Cyp1a2. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Gemfibrozil may influence Cyp1a2 activity, though the direct interaction between Gemfibrozil and Cyp1a2 remains less clear. \n\nThe evidence also shows that Gemfibrozil resembles Bupranolol and Clenbuterol, both of which bind to Cyp1a2. This structural similarity may explain the observed interaction, though the exact mechanism of how Gemfibrozil influences Cyp1a2 is not fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Gemfibrozil to Cyp1a2 through different metabolic processes highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the core mechanism likely involves the modulation of Cyp1a2 activity through interactions with Cyp2c9 or other enzymes involved in substrate oxidation.",
